From: Joan Karadimov <joan.karadimov@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Do not hand a detached child this process's console

buildPackageList() ends by firing off

    pacman --print-format "%n %v %s" -Spu

through execCommandInAnotherThread(), and nothing ever reads the result --
startDetached() returns immediately and the QProcess goes out of scope. But a
detached child inherits the parent's stdout and stderr, so on a system with
updates pending those lines are printed to whatever console octopi was
started from, on every start. Here that is 94 lines.

Two things were wrong. p.startDetached(cmd, params) is the *static* overload
reached through an instance, so nothing configured on p applied; the member
overload is the one that honours redirections. And nothing was redirected.
Both are fixed by setting the program and arguments on p, pointing its output
at the null device, and calling the member overload.

Not Windows-specific: the same lines go to the terminal on Linux. They are
just rarely seen there, because octopi is usually started from a desktop
menu with no console attached.

Worth sending upstream.
diff --git a/src/globals.cpp b/src/globals.cpp
index 0364694..1836d93 100644
--- a/src/globals.cpp
+++ b/src/globals.cpp
@@ -217,7 +217,19 @@ QByteArray execCommand(QString cmd)
 void execCommandInAnotherThread(QString cmd, QStringList &params)
 {
   QProcess p;
-  p.startDetached(cmd, params);
+  p.setProgram(cmd);
+  p.setArguments(params);
+  // A detached child is handed this process's own stdout and stderr, and
+  // nothing here ever reads them -- the call is fire-and-forget. So the 94
+  // lines of "pacman --print-format %n %v %s -Spu" land in whatever console
+  // octopi was started from, every time it starts.
+  //
+  // Note this was p.startDetached(cmd, params), which is the *static*
+  // overload reached through an instance: everything configured on p was
+  // being ignored. The member overload is what honours these.
+  p.setStandardOutputFile(QProcess::nullDevice());
+  p.setStandardErrorFile(QProcess::nullDevice());
+  p.startDetached();
 }
 
